"""
citers -- every work that cites a paper, from three open citation indexes,
merged into one list and checked against your BibTeX files and your notes.

Usage:
    citers DOI [options]

Sources (all free, no account needed):
    OpenAlex           filter=cites:<work>
    OpenCitations      index v2 (its arXiv-only and PubMed-only rows are named
                       through the arXiv API and PubMed)
    Semantic Scholar   citations, with the sentences that cite (--contexts)
Preprints are joined to their published version through the doi arXiv records
for them; works are also joined by DOI, PubMed id and normalised title.
Crossref's own count of citing works is printed as a check on coverage.

Options:
    -b, --bib FILES       BibTeX file(s), comma-separated: citing works are
                          given the key they have there (DOI, arXiv id, title)
    -k, --known FILE      a text holding the keys already accounted for, e.g.
                          a LaTeX file or wiki source ("-" = stdin). Keys are
                          read from \\cite{..}, {{key}}, {{cite|a,b}} and the
                          like; with --bib only real bib keys count
    -w, --wiki-page TITLE read the known keys from a MediaWiki page instead
        --wiki-api URL    that wiki's api.php (or env CITERS_WIKI_API)
    -o, --own NAMES       surnames, comma-separated, marking self-citations
                          ("Laussy,del Valle"); shown with a * and counted apart
    -s, --since YEAR      only citing works from YEAR on
    -m, --missing         only works not among the known keys (or, without
                          --known, not in the bib files)
    -f, --format FMT      text (default), csv, json, keys (bib keys, one per
                          line), ids (DOI or arXiv:ID of works with no key --
                          ready for a doi-to-bibtex tool)
        --contexts        under each work, the sentences that cite (Semantic
                          Scholar; often taken from the arXiv version)
        --hunt QUERY      also look for citations the indexes failed to link:
                          works matching QUERY in title/abstract (OpenAlex)
                          are kept if their Crossref reference list cites the
                          paper. Repeatable
        --hunt-since YEAR start of the hunt (default: the paper's year)
        --hunt-max N      candidates checked per query (default 300)
        --mailto EMAIL    contact for the OpenAlex/Crossref polite pools
                          (or env CITERS_MAILTO); nothing is sent without it
        --s2-key KEY      Semantic Scholar API key (or env S2_API_KEY);
                          without one, rate limits are met by waiting
    -q, --quiet           no progress or summary on stderr
    -V, --version         the version
    -h, --help            this message

Status column: K known, b in a bib file but not known, N new (no key).
Sources column: A OpenAlex, C OpenCitations, S Semantic Scholar,
X found by --hunt in a Crossref reference list.
"""

